temological implications. It is concluded that the standard theory remains the only one which is compatible with present quantum mechanics. Hence, if one wants to avoid the conclusion that quantum mechanics only gives probability connections between subsequent observations, the quantum-mechanical equations would have to be modified. Particular attention is paid to the case that the measuring apparatus is macroscopic and its state vector not accurately known before the measurement.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "submitter"}}], "titles": [{"source": "submitter", "title": "The Problem of Measurement"}], "facet_author_name": ["983578_Eugene P. Wigner"], "core": false, "imprints": [{"date": "1963-01"}], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:1777593", "updated": "2023-03-07T05:32:47.859264"}, "curated": false, "journal_title_variants": ["Am. J. Phys.", "Am.J.Phys."]}, "updated": "2023-03-07T05:32:47.859264+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1119%2F1.1969254&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1119%2F1.1969254&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1119%2F1.1969254&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1119%2F1.1969254&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1119%2F1.1969254&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1119%2F1.1969254&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1119%2F1.1969254&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}